          <p>St Helens has a big share of Victorian and Edwardian terraced housing, especially across WA10. These homes were built with gravity-fed water systems using cold tanks in the loft. In freezing weather, loft tanks and their pipes can freeze and burst. The risk is highest where insulation was laid over the tank, not under it. Our engineers know these systems and know exactly what to look for on a burst pipe call in the older parts of St Helens town.</p>
